  "body": "I'm looking at [create an element for the token](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#create-an-element-for-the-token) step 7, it has a note:\n\n\"This will cause custom element constructors to run, if will execute script is true. However, even if this causes new characters to be inserted into the tokenizer, the parser will not be executed reentrantly, since the parser pause flag is true. Similarly, blowing away the document is not possible, since the script nesting level is greater than zero.\"\n\nThat nomenclature&mdash;reentrantly&mdash;is a bit confusing. [document.write](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-document-write) step 7 says:\n\n\"If there is no pending parsing-blocking script, ...\" (parse the content)\n\nThere's a note describing this as reentrant invocation of the parser.\n\nMaybe the note could be more specific about the relationship between the parser blocking script, tokenization and the parser pause flag. That is, a parser blocking script is only _set_ when processing an end script tag token; if the tokenizer is blocked, then the parser blocking script cannot be set. (I hope that is right?)\n",
